WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.637 --> 00:00:14.217
left Mr.

2
00:00:14.237 --> 00:00:15.038
Pendleton's house.

3
00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:20.220
As she walked down Pendleton Hill, the sky was filled with storm clouds.

4
00:00:23.321 --> 00:00:25.342
Soon she met Nancy carrying an umbrella.

5
00:00:25.362 --> 00:00:29.264
"Miss Polly was worried you'd get soaked in the rain."

6
00:00:30.376 --> 00:00:32.338
"Oh, I didn't mean to scare her."

7
00:00:32.358 --> 00:00:37.662
"Well, I'm glad she was worried," Nancy said.

8
00:00:38.803 --> 00:00:41.305
Pollyanna was so shocked, she stopped walking.

9
00:00:42.406 --> 00:00:45.269
"Glad that Aunt Polly was worried about me?

10
00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.232
Oh, Nancy, that's not how we play the game."

11
00:00:49.252 --> 00:00:53.876
"I wasn't playing the game," Nancy said sharply.

12
00:00:53.896 --> 00:00:58.340
"You don't appreciate what it means that Miss Polly was worried about you.

13
00:00:59.612 --> 00:01:02.234
It means she's becoming human!

14
00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:05.556
She's not just doing her duty all the time.

15
00:01:06.877 --> 00:01:09.239
And she's a better person since you arrived.

16
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.983
She took in that dog and cat, and she's much nicer to me."

17
00:01:16.904 --> 00:01:18.045
Pollyanna hesitated.

18
00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:22.088
"Do you think Aunt Polly likes that I live with her?

19
00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:24.950
Would she miss me if I left?"

20
00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:27.632
"Of course she'd miss you!

21
00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:30.725
She sent me out with this umbrella.

22
00:01:31.805 --> 00:01:33.785
And she moved you to that pretty bedroom."

23
00:01:35.366 --> 00:01:37.406
Nancy knew her words would please Pollyanna.

24
00:01:38.487 --> 00:01:41.968
But she wasn't prepared for the sudden joy that illuminated Pollyanna's face.

25
00:01:46.089 --> 00:01:48.370
Pollyanna skipped the rest of the way home.

26
00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:52.891
"I couldn't leave Aunt Polly now," she thought.

27
00:01:52.911 --> 00:01:56.392
"I always knew I wanted to live with her.

28
00:01:57.804 --> 00:02:01.745
But I didn't know how much I wanted Aunt Polly to want to live with me!"

29
00:02:04.986 --> 00:02:07.967
The next day Pollyanna walked back up Pendleton Hill.

30
00:02:09.748 --> 00:02:11.128
She dreaded telling Mr.

31
00:02:11.188 --> 00:02:13.809
Pendleton of her decision to stay with Aunt Polly.

32
00:02:15.029 --> 00:02:17.870
She felt sorry that he lived such a sad, lonely life.

33
00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:23.852
And she suspected that the big, gray house would become cluttered and dusty again.

34
00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:32.798
"If only there was someone else Oh, I have an idea!"

35
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:36.861
She hurried into Mr.

36
00:02:36.921 --> 00:02:40.684
Pendleton's library, where a cheery fire glowed in the fireplace.

37
00:02:42.106 --> 00:02:44.628
"I've thought of the gladdest thing you could do!"

38
00:02:44.648 --> 00:02:46.790
"With you?"

39
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.952
Mr. Pendleton said cautiously.

40
00:02:48.972 --> 00:02:53.756
"No, but—" "You're turning down my offer?"

41
00:02:55.392 --> 00:02:56.373
Pollyanna nodded.

42
00:02:56.393 --> 00:03:00.897
"Aunt Polly—" "Did she refuse to let you come?"

43
00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:04.940
"I—I didn't ask her.

44
00:03:06.141 --> 00:03:10.684
I couldn't ask her after I accidentally found out she wants me with her.

45
00:03:11.845 --> 00:03:13.487
And I want to stay too.

46
00:03:14.988 --> 00:03:19.151
She's starting to be glad about a lot of things, so I can't leave her now."

47
00:03:21.393 --> 00:03:25.056
There was a long pause with only the crackling fire to break the silence.

48
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.401
"I'm disappointed, but I won't ask you again."

49
00:03:28.902 --> 00:03:31.063
Mr. Pendleton spoke in a low voice.

50
00:03:31.083 --> 00:03:33.644
"I have a new idea!

51
00:03:34.605 --> 00:03:39.307
You want a partner's hand and heart or a child's presence to make this house a home.

52
00:03:40.508 --> 00:03:42.969
Well, I know another child you could adopt!"

53
00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.452
Mr. Pendleton looked outraged by her suggestion.

54
00:03:47.472 --> 00:03:51.194
"I don't want another child."

55
00:03:51.214 --> 00:03:54.696
"But you're so kind to other people.

56
00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.308
You gave prisms to Mrs.

57
00:03:57.429 --> 00:04:02.090
Snow and me, a gold coin to Nancy, money to orphans overseas."

58
00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.291
"Pollyanna, listen!"

59
00:04:04.671 --> 00:04:06.271
Mr. Pendleton said sharply.

60
00:04:06.291 --> 00:04:12.553
"I've never sent a penny to orphans overseas, and those other gifts were your ideas."

61
00:04:13.974 --> 00:04:17.095
Mr. Pendleton expected Pollyanna to be disappointed in him.

62
00:04:18.615 --> 00:04:20.956
Instead she gleefully clapped her hands.

63
00:04:22.216 --> 00:04:23.536
"I'm so glad!

64
00:04:23.957 --> 00:04:27.037
I mean, I'm not glad that you've sent nothing to the orphans.

65
00:04:27.998 --> 00:04:29.878
But I'm glad you can help Jimmy Bean."

66
00:04:29.898 --> 00:04:32.099
"Who's Jimmy Bean?"

67
00:04:32.119 --> 00:04:36.920
"The 'child's presence' that's going to make this place a home.

68
00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:39.401
Poor Jimmy!

69
00:04:39.941 --> 00:04:43.022
I had to tell him that my Ladies' Aid out West wouldn't take him.

70
00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:45.923
He'll be so glad to come here!"

71
00:04:45.943 --> 00:04:49.904
"Pollyanna, this is nonsense!"

72
00:04:51.508 --> 00:04:53.529
"You mean you won't take him?"

73
00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:55.730
Pollyanna was stunned.

74
00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.772
"Correct." "Fine!

75
00:05:00.212 --> 00:05:02.973
I'll find someone else who wants a nice little boy."

76
00:05:04.194 --> 00:05:07.255
Tears of frustration streamed down Pollyanna's face.

77
00:05:07.275 --> 00:05:11.737
"I didn't even get to say he's willing to work."

78
00:05:14.778 --> 00:05:16.599
Moved by her tears, Mr.

79
00:05:16.639 --> 00:05:17.920
Pendleton spoke gently.

80
00:05:19.488 --> 00:05:21.989
"Why don't you tell me more about this nice little boy?"

81
00:05:27.052 --> 00:05:29.854
The next Saturday Pollyanna and Jimmy visited Mr.

82
00:05:29.894 --> 00:05:34.696
Pendleton. Jimmy was wary about meeting another of Pollyanna's friends.

83
00:05:38.258 --> 00:05:43.001
Having been rejected by Aunt Polly and two Ladies' Aid groups, he wasn't exactly rude.

84
00:05:44.201 --> 00:05:44.782
But when Mr.

85
00:05:44.822 --> 00:05:48.664
Pendleton asked him questions, he looked away and gave short answers.

86
00:05:50.304 --> 00:05:52.226
He never once smiled or thanked Mr.

87
00:05:52.246 --> 00:05:53.827
Pendleton for inviting him to visit.

88
00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:00.132
After Jimmy left, Pollyanna turned to Mr.

89
00:06:00.152 --> 00:06:04.215
Pendleton. "So, are you going to adopt him?"

90
00:06:04.235 --> 00:06:06.918
"I'll think about it," Mr.

91
00:06:06.938 --> 00:06:07.858
Pendleton replied.

92
00:06:10.781 --> 00:06:11.762
Pollyanna sighed.

93
00:06:11.782 --> 00:06:14.484
That probably meant no.
